        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: normalize unsupported Anthropic inline images",
        "body": "Closes #102323\n\n## Summary\n\n- normalize unsupported Anthropic inline image MIME types at the payload boundary instead of forwarding `image/heic` / `image/tiff` verbatim\n- keep `@openclaw/ai` package-independent by routing packaged-provider normalization through the optional AI transport host port, with OpenClaw core injecting the shared implementation\n- reuse the same byte-aware normalization path for packaged Anthropic user/tool-result payloads and the custom Anthropic transport\n- prefer detected byte format over declared MIME so mislabeled or missing metadata cannot bypass conversion; fall back to a supported declaration only when byte detection is inconclusive\n- preserve text-only and non-vision fast paths, with focused regressions for provider, transport, and declared-versus-detected MIME behavior\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/ai/src/providers/anthropic.test.ts src/agents/anthropic-transport-stream.test.ts src/media/anthropic-inline-images.test.ts` (184 tests passed across 3 shards)\n- `node_modules/oxfmt/bin/oxfmt --check packages/ai/src/host.ts packages/ai/src/providers/anthropic.test.ts packages/ai/src/providers/anthropic.ts src/agents/anthropic-transport-stream.test.ts src/agents/anthropic-transport-stream.ts src/llm/ai-transport-host.ts src/media/anthropic-inline-images.test.ts src/media/anthropic-inline-images.ts src/media/image-ops.ts`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n- `node scripts/build-all.mjs` (passed with Node 22.22.3 and Corepack pnpm 11.2.2; full tsdown, plugin assets, SDK export guard, runtime postbuild, and Control UI build)\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main --codex-bin /Applications/ChatGPT.app/Contents/Resources/codex --stream-engine-output` (clean; no accepted/actionable findings, correctness 0.84)\n- `node --import tsx /private/tmp/openclaw-102323-proof-current.ts` (exact-head loopback payload proof passed)\n- refreshed from current `upstream/main` `0a19e1ed58632e82148409550e3a245653aeb179`; exact tested head `a172460032212eb858ecb2f190fe465cdeb5ef50`\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed: Anthropic user-image and tool-result payloads no longer send unsupported `image/heic` / `image/tiff` media types verbatim; they normalize to `image/jpeg` before the request leaves OpenClaw. The normalizer now also checks the actual byte format before trusting a supported declaration.\n\nReal environment tested: Exact head `a172460032212eb858ecb2f190fe465cdeb5ef50` on macOS arm64 and Node 22.22.3. The run used the real `streamAnthropic()` packaged provider with OpenClaw's AI transport host wiring and the real `createAnthropicMessagesTransportStreamFn()` custom transport against a temporary `127.0.0.1` Anthropic-compatible capture server that recorded outbound `/v1/messages` payloads and returned Anthropic-style SSE responses.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch: `node --import tsx /private/tmp/openclaw-102323-proof-current.ts`\n\nEvidence after fix:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"head\": \"a1724600322\",\n  \"captured\": [\n    { \"caseId\": \"packaged-user-heic\", \"mediaType\": \"image/jpeg\" },\n    { \"caseId\": \"packaged-tool-tiff\", \"mediaType\": \"image/jpeg\" },\n    { \"caseId\": \"transport-user-heic\", \"mediaType\": \"image/jpeg\" }\n  ],\n  \"packagedResult\": { \"stopReason\": \"stop\", \"errorMessage\": \"\" },\n  \"packagedToolResult\": { \"stopReason\": \"stop\", \"errorMessage\": \"\" },\n  \"transportResult\": { \"stopReason\": \"stop\", \"errorMessage\": \"\" }\n}\n```\n\nObserved result after fix: The packaged Anthropic provider sent both the HEIC user-image case and TIFF tool-result case as `image/jpeg`; the custom Anthropic transport sent the HEIC user-image case as `image/jpeg`. All three requests completed successfully through the real OpenClaw payload builders and returned `stopReason: stop` with no error.\n\nWhat was not tested: Live `api.anthropic.com` was not called; the proof swaps only the remote endpoint for a loopback capture server. It does not exercise wider upstream session/image ingestion beyond these Anthropic request builders. Actual declared-versus-detected mismatch conversion is covered by the focused byte-sniffing regression rather than the loopback run.\n",
        "branch": "fix/anthropic-heic-tiff-media-type",
